// 인용은 notes/web/<id>.txt 에 글자 그대로 있다(공백 차이 제외). 그림 글자는 notes/figures.md 에 있고 source 는 그 그림이 실린 w1 이다.
{"id": "e1", "source": "w1", "locator": "§intro bullets", "quote": "A structured, auditable knowledge architecture separates what the agent knows from how it reasons.", "why": "B 의 두 층 중 첫째"}
{"id": "e2", "source": "w1", "locator": "§intro bullets", "quote": "A self-improvement loop then compiles expert feedback into verified, regression-tested updates without model retraining.", "why": "B 의 두 층 중 둘째, 재학습 없음"}
{"id": "e3", "source": "w1", "locator": "§intro bullets", "quote": "the pattern is designed to generalize to other domains governed by retrievable text rather than model weights", "why": "일반화 조건: 가중치가 아니라 텍스트로 통제되는 영역"}
{"id": "e4", "source": "w1", "locator": "§intro", "quote": "In compliance domains, for example, the same types of questions can arise across hundreds of product reviews, expert assessments take days of manual research, and inconsistency between assessments creates real organizational risk.", "why": "problem: 같은 질문 반복, 며칠, 불일치"}
{"id": "e5", "source": "w1", "locator": "§The Architecture at a Glance", "quote": "it will not be able to distinguish between what an organization could do (a summary of general information) and what it should consider doing (based on historic positions, company direction, business context, etc.)", "why": "범용 LLM 의 한계: could vs should"}
{"id": "e6", "source": "w1", "locator": "§The Architecture at a Glance", "quote": "The knowledge system’s file structure makes automated editing possible. The reasoning layer’s explicit procedures make failure attribution tractable. The evaluation framework gates every change.", "why": "네 층의 상호 의존"}
{"id": "e7", "source": "w1", "locator": "§The Architecture at a Glance", "quote": "Remove any one layer and the others degrade.", "why": "층 하나를 빼면 나머지가 약해진다"}
{"id": "e8", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Building the Organizational Second Brain", "quote": "An agent that retrieves document chunks at inference time has to re-derive that reasoning from raw sources on every run, which is slow, error-prone, and inconsistent.", "why": "chunk RAG 의 문제 정의"}
{"id": "e9", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Building the Organizational Second Brain", "quote": "A long-running offline process reasons through source documents and distills them into structured knowledge files", "why": "오프라인 증류"}
{"id": "e10", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Building the Organizational Second Brain", "quote": "Andrej Karpathy’s LLM Wiki structures agent knowledge as a navigable graph of files, and Google’s Open Knowledge Format standardizes this for cross-agent interoperability.", "why": "B 가 스스로 대는 계보"}
{"id": "e11", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Building the Organizational Second Brain", "quote": "We extended these principles into a system where citation fidelity and institutional consistency are non-negotiable, organizing 200+ files into a strict taxonomy:", "why": "200+ files 숫자"}
{"id": "e12", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Building the Organizational Second Brain", "quote": "Position files capture authoritative organizational stances: how the organization has decided to interpret a given domain question, along with its constraints, boundary conditions, and machine-actionable routing implications", "why": "position 파일 정의"}
{"id": "e13", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Building the Organizational Second Brain", "quote": "Taxonomy and vocabulary files act as an authoritative glossary for the terms the organization uses to describe its domain", "why": "vocabulary 파일 정의"}
{"id": "e14", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Building the Organizational Second Brain", "quote": "Routing indexes map input characteristics to the relevant positions and procedures, determining which files apply without relying on embedding similarity alone. This makes retrieval deterministic and auditable.", "why": "routing index 정의"}
{"id": "e15", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Building the Organizational Second Brain", "quote": "Gateway files define threshold tests the agent must pass before entering an analytical domain, preventing it from applying specialized knowledge where it does not belong.", "why": "gateway 파일 정의"}
{"id": "e16", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Building the Organizational Second Brain", "quote": "Every file declares its dependencies (depends_on) and consumers (referenced_by) in YAML frontmatter, forming a bidirectional dependency graph.", "why": "양방향 의존 그래프"}
{"id": "e17", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Building the Organizational Second Brain", "quote": "When one file changes, you can trace exactly what else might be affected, which matters when the self-improvement loop proposes automated edits.", "why": "의존 그래프가 자동 편집의 전제"}
{"id": "e18", "source": "w1", "locator": "w1 knowledge-system 그림", "quote": "triggers: # WHEN to load this page", "why": "frontmatter 의 triggers 필드"}
{"id": "e19", "source": "w1", "locator": "w1 knowledge-system 그림", "quote": "SKILL.md ← \"Homepage\" — routes to the right workflow", "why": "그림의 진입 파일 이름이 SKILL.md"}
{"id": "e20", "source": "w1", "locator": "w1 knowledge-system 그림", "quote": "knowledge/positions/ ← Supreme authority articles", "why": "position 이 최상위 권위"}
{"id": "e21", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Organizing Knowledge by Density and Usage Frequency", "quote": "We split on information density and expected usage frequency.", "why": "분할 기준"}
{"id": "e22", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Organizing Knowledge by Density and Usage Frequency", "quote": "High-density, frequently referenced sources go into the wiki: Distilled files capturing how the organization reasons, such as positions, decision frameworks, boundary examples, and strategic interpretations. The agent consults these on nearly every turn.", "why": "wiki 쪽"}
{"id": "e23", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Organizing Knowledge by Density and Usage Frequency", "quote": "Sparse, situationally relevant sources are served through semantic or lexical search (RAG): documents that matter deeply when they apply but are not needed in detail on most runs", "why": "RAG 쪽"}
{"id": "e24", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Organizing Knowledge by Density and Usage Frequency", "quote": "Loading all of them into the wiki would bloat the system and dilute attention.", "why": "전부 wiki 에 넣지 않는 이유"}
{"id": "e25", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Expert Reasoning via Composable Recipes", "quote": "Where knowledge files are declarative, recipes are imperative.", "why": "recipe 정의"}
{"id": "e26", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Expert Reasoning via Composable Recipes", "quote": "Recipes reference knowledge files but contain no domain facts; knowledge files state positions but prescribe no procedures.", "why": "분리 규칙"}
{"id": "e27", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Expert Reasoning via Composable Recipes", "quote": "Adding an organizational position means adding a knowledge file and updating a routing index. No recipe changes.", "why": "변경 국소성 1"}
{"id": "e28", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Expert Reasoning via Composable Recipes", "quote": "Fixing a flaw in the agent’s methodology means editing a recipe. No knowledge files change.", "why": "변경 국소성 2"}
{"id": "e29", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Expert Reasoning via Composable Recipes", "quote": "Failures attribute cleanly to one layer. Was the knowledge wrong, or the procedure?", "why": "귀속 가능성"}
{"id": "e30", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Expert Reasoning via Composable Recipes", "quote": "Our top-level routing recipe examines the input and selects which downstream recipes to invoke, each handling one analytical phase.", "why": "routing recipe"}
{"id": "e31", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Expert Reasoning via Composable Recipes", "quote": "Early versions used a single flat instruction file and loaded all sources via semantic search, pulling a large volume of mixed-relevance files into the context window on every run.", "why": "이전 구조"}
{"id": "e32", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Expert Reasoning via Composable Recipes", "quote": "After restructuring into recipe-driven stages, each query touches only a small, targeted subset, cutting tokens consumed per turn by around 80%.", "why": "80% 숫자와 비교 기준"}
{"id": "e33", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Keeping Humans in Control", "quote": "Checkpoints are defined points in the analysis where the agent surfaces its intermediate reasoning for expert review before proceeding, and the expert can confirm, correct, or redirect.", "why": "checkpoint"}
{"id": "e34", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Keeping Humans in Control", "quote": "Escalations trigger when the agent hits genuine ambiguity, whether from underspecified inputs or evidence that supports more than one defensible reading.", "why": "escalation"}
{"id": "e35", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Keeping Humans in Control", "quote": "Training signal: Every correction and every escalation becomes input for the self-improvement loop.", "why": "교정이 루프 입력"}
{"id": "e36", "source": "w1", "locator": "§The Self-Improvement Flywheel", "quote": "This process can take weeks because it requires understanding the full dependency graph, verifying nothing else breaks, and validating the fix actually works.", "why": "수작업 유지보수 비용"}
{"id": "e37", "source": "w1", "locator": "§The Self-Improvement Flywheel", "quote": "Agents that auto-draft their own fixes are increasingly common; but we haven’t seen this level of validation rigor applied to a structured knowledge base without model retraining.", "why": "B 의 새로움 주장"}
{"id": "e38", "source": "w1", "locator": "§The Self-Improvement Flywheel", "quote": "We treat that maintenance as a compilation problem and automate it.", "why": "compilation 비유"}
{"id": "e39", "source": "w1", "locator": "§The Self-Improvement Flywheel", "quote": "Have domain experts review them.", "why": "본문 목록 넷째 phase 는 사람 검토"}
{"id": "e40", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Diagnosis", "quote": "This heuristic failed because conversational form is a poor proxy for root cause.", "why": "첫 접근의 실패"}
{"id": "e41", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Diagnosis", "quote": "First, extract every substantive signal from the expert alongside the agent’s full knowledge manifest (every file loaded, when, and how used).", "why": "manifest"}
{"id": "e42", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Diagnosis", "quote": "Could the agent have reached the correct conclusion from its source materials?", "why": "귀속 테스트 질문"}
{"id": "e43", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Diagnosis", "quote": "If the materials contained the right answer but the agent still erred: recipe problem.", "why": "분기 1"}
{"id": "e44", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Diagnosis", "quote": "If the materials did not contain the right answer: knowledge gap.", "why": "분기 2"}
{"id": "e45", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Diagnosis", "quote": "If experts themselves disagree on the right answer: ambiguity, flagged for human discussion.", "why": "분기 3"}
{"id": "e46", "source": "w1", "locator": "w1 루프 그림 Phase 1", "quote": "Weight By Frequency And Severity", "why": "그림에만 있는 가중 단계"}
{"id": "e47", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Compilation", "quote": "Sub-agents analyze impact in parallel, examining cross-references, conflicts with existing positions, token budget impact, test coverage, and duplication risk.", "why": "병렬 영향 분석"}
{"id": "e48", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Compilation", "quote": "A separate agent, running in a fresh context with no knowledge of the improvement rationale, receives only the proposed diffs to the knowledge base.", "why": "적대적 리뷰어 입력"}
{"id": "e49", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Compilation", "quote": "Because it shares no context with the proposing agents, it cannot inherit their blind spots.", "why": "분리의 이유"}
{"id": "e50", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Compilation", "quote": "A linter catches issues programmatically, dangling cross-references, file size budget violations, identifier collisions, and dependency cycles. This layer is not probabilistic. It passes or fails.", "why": "결정적 linter"}
{"id": "e51", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Evaluation", "quote": "Targeted replay runs the agent on the original scenario that triggered the feedback. The agent does not know it is being tested.", "why": "targeted replay"}
{"id": "e52", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Evaluation", "quote": "A separate judge evaluates the new output against the original expert feedback without knowing what was changed.", "why": "blind judge"}
{"id": "e53", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Evaluation", "quote": "Regression testing runs multiple benchmarks for that domain, which are usually structured test suites of Q&A pairs.", "why": "회귀 벤치마크 형태"}
{"id": "e54", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Evaluation", "quote": "an independent LLM judge gives each test case a pass/fail based on certain criteria", "why": "판정자도 LLM"}
{"id": "e55", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Evaluation", "quote": "If regression testing fails, compilation is retried with an updated prompt describing where the agent regressed, along with the original issue and attempted fix.", "why": "재시도 프롬프트"}
{"id": "e56", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Landing and Enrichment", "quote": "The output of the pipeline is a pull request (diff) with a complete audit trail. A human expert reviews a proven fix rather than debugging a raw failure.", "why": "PR 로 착지"}
{"id": "e57", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Landing and Enrichment", "quote": "the original failing scenario and its validated correct answer are automatically added to the regression test suite", "why": "보강"}
{"id": "e58", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Results", "quote": "After three development sprints spanning six weeks, the system achieved:", "why": "결과 기간"}
{"id": "e59", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Results", "quote": "Domain SMEs rated agent outputs useful almost all the time", "why": "결과 1 정성"}
{"id": "e60", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Results", "quote": "Days to minutes reduction in individual assessment time.", "why": "결과 2"}
{"id": "e61", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Results", "quote": "Automated self-improvement producing validated knowledge edits at a rate that previously required full engineering sprints.", "why": "결과 3"}
{"id": "e62", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Results", "quote": "Zero regressions across improvement cycles, with every fix automatically strengthening the regression suite.", "why": "결과 4"}
{"id": "e63", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Applying This Architecture", "quote": "Specialist knowledge lives as tribal knowledge in experts’ heads.", "why": "적용 조건 1"}
{"id": "e64", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Applying This Architecture", "quote": "Off-the-shelf LLMs produce inadequate analysis.", "why": "적용 조건 4"}
{"id": "e65", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Applying This Architecture", "quote": "keep the complexity in text files that are readable by both humans and agents, rather than fine-tuned model weights", "why": "핵심 원리"}
{"id": "e66", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Applying This Architecture", "quote": "Every improvement is a text edit that a domain expert can review in 30 seconds. Every change is version-controlled, diffable, and reversible.", "why": "30초, 버전 관리"}
{"id": "e67", "source": "w2", "locator": "§Code is no longer the bottleneck", "quote": "Build is no longer the constraint — the human-speed steps around it are.", "why": "playbook 의 전제"}
{"id": "e68", "source": "w2", "locator": "§What is an AI-native SDLC?", "quote": "The AI-native SDLC is a reimagined process that combines the old control objectives with new enforcement. Instead of a linear flow, the process becomes a loop, and AI is embedded at each point.", "why": "정의"}
{"id": "e69", "source": "w2", "locator": "§What is an AI-native SDLC?", "quote": "The thread running through the right-hand column is the committed artifact.", "why": "committed artifact"}
{"id": "e70", "source": "w2", "locator": "§What is an AI-native SDLC?", "quote": "The chain of commits is also the audit trail: who asked for what, what the agent produced, and who approved it.", "why": "audit trail"}
{"id": "e71", "source": "w2", "locator": "§Build · The CLAUDE.md", "quote": "Knowledge that used to sit in people's heads and on wikis becomes a file the agent reads at the start of every session, maintained by the whole team and iterated on whenever a mistake is made.", "why": "CLAUDE.md 가 지식 파일"}
{"id": "e72", "source": "w2", "locator": "§Build · The CLAUDE.md", "quote": "When Claude makes a mistake twice, the correction goes into CLAUDE.md.", "why": "두 번 규칙"}
{"id": "e73", "source": "w2", "locator": "§Build · The CLAUDE.md", "quote": "Keep it under a page, because Claude reads all of it at the start of a session and anything stale is taking up context for no benefit.", "why": "한 쪽 이하"}
{"id": "e74", "source": "w2", "locator": "§Build · Skills as institutional knowledge", "quote": "Skills are how an organization makes its institutional knowledge operational. The instructions are explicit, version-controlled, applied broadly, and updated centrally when policy changes.", "why": "skills 가 제도 지식"}
{"id": "e75", "source": "w2", "locator": "§Build · Skills as institutional knowledge", "quote": "Write it as a skill, a folder containing a SKILL.md whose frontmatter says when it triggers and whose body says what to do.", "why": "SKILL.md frontmatter trigger"}
{"id": "e76", "source": "w2", "locator": "§Build · Skills as institutional knowledge", "quote": "When the policy changes, change the skill and have the policy owner sign off the change.", "why": "정책 소유자 서명"}
{"id": "e77", "source": "w2", "locator": "§Build · Skills as institutional knowledge", "quote": "A skill is a control, though an advisory one. It makes Claude likely to apply the policy while the code is written, and nothing forces a session to comply with it.", "why": "advisory control"}
{"id": "e78", "source": "w2", "locator": "§Build · Skills as institutional knowledge", "quote": "Where the findings don't fall towards zero, either the skill isn't triggering or its text has drifted from the official policy.", "why": "skill drift 측정"}
{"id": "e79", "source": "w2", "locator": "§Test · Give Claude a feedback loop", "quote": "This way the verdict is not colored by the assumptions that produced the code.", "why": "fresh context verifier"}
{"id": "e80", "source": "w2", "locator": "§Test · Give Claude a feedback loop", "quote": "Finally, the loop itself needs protecting, because an agent fixing code must not be able to weaken the check on that code.", "why": "검사 보호"}
{"id": "e81", "source": "w2", "locator": "§Test · Continuous evals in CI", "quote": "When a new model is swapped in or a prompt is rewritten, the eval suite says whether the agent still does the work to the same standard.", "why": "config 회귀"}
{"id": "e82", "source": "w2", "locator": "§Test · Continuous evals in CI", "quote": "The platform engineer collects 20 to 50 real tasks from recent work with its expected/accepted outcome.", "why": "eval 규모"}
{"id": "e83", "source": "w2", "locator": "§Test · Continuous evals in CI", "quote": "The suite runs non-interactively in CI on a schedule and on any change to CLAUDE.md, skills or hooks, since that configuration steers the agent and deserves the regression testing that code gets.", "why": "설정도 회귀 테스트"}
{"id": "e84", "source": "w2", "locator": "§Test · Continuous evals in CI", "quote": "Each production incident gets an eval, written by the team that owned the incident, and stays in the suite as a regression test.", "why": "incident → eval"}
{"id": "e85", "source": "w2", "locator": "§Test · Continuous evals in CI", "quote": "As models improve, cases that once discriminated stop doing so and new ones must be added that arise from ongoing monitoring.", "why": "eval 수명"}
{"id": "e86", "source": "w2", "locator": "§Deploy · AI in the PR review loop", "quote": "Separation of duties is preserved, because the agent that wrote the code has no way to approve it.", "why": "직무 분리"}
{"id": "e87", "source": "w2", "locator": "§Deploy · AI in the PR review loop", "quote": "Review findings feed back into CLAUDE.md. When a review flags a mistake for the second time, the correction goes into CLAUDE.md as part of that review", "why": "리뷰 → CLAUDE.md"}
{"id": "e88", "source": "w2", "locator": "§Deploy · CI/CD integration and deployment", "quote": "Rollback should be the most rehearsed path in the pipeline", "why": "rollback"}
{"id": "e89", "source": "w2", "locator": "§Maintain", "quote": "Stage 6: Maintenance runs headless, with an independent confidence gate between stages, a deterministic check or an adversarial reviewing agent, deciding whether the previous stage's output continues or is escalated to a human.", "why": "독립 confidence gate"}
{"id": "e90", "source": "w2", "locator": "§Maintain · Closing the loop", "quote": "The script is version controlled and unit tested, and detection stays entirely deterministic, with no model involved.", "why": "결정적 탐지"}
{"id": "e91", "source": "w2", "locator": "§Maintain · Closing the loop", "quote": "When a fix ships, add an eval for the incident (the continuous evals play) to ensure that such issues are protected against going forwards.", "why": "fix → eval"}
{"id": "e92", "source": "w2", "locator": "§Closing thoughts", "quote": "The loop keeps running. Human judgement stays above it.", "why": "맺음"}
{"id": "e93", "source": "w3", "locator": "§The core idea", "quote": "The knowledge is compiled once and then *kept current*, not re-derived on every query.", "why": "LLM Wiki 핵심"}
{"id": "e94", "source": "w3", "locator": "§Architecture", "quote": "**The schema** — a document (e.g. CLAUDE.md for Claude Code or AGENTS.md for Codex) that tells the LLM how the wiki is structured", "why": "schema 층"}
{"id": "e95", "source": "w3", "locator": "§Operations", "quote": "**Lint.** Periodically, ask the LLM to health-check the wiki. Look for: contradictions between pages, stale claims that newer sources have superseded, orphan pages with no inbound links", "why": "Karpathy 의 lint"}
{"id": "e96", "source": "w3", "locator": "§Indexing and logging", "quote": "This works surprisingly well at moderate scale (~100 sources, ~hundreds of pages) and avoids the need for embedding-based RAG infrastructure.", "why": "index 로 충분한 규모"}
{"id": "e97", "source": "w3", "locator": "§Why this works", "quote": "The wiki stays maintained because the cost of maintenance is near zero.", "why": "유지비 주장"}
{"id": "e98", "source": "w3", "locator": "§The core idea", "quote": "You never (or rarely) write the wiki yourself — the LLM writes and maintains all of it.", "why": "LLM 이 소유"}
{"id": "e99", "source": "w4", "locator": "§intro", "quote": "an open specification that formalizes the LLM-wiki pattern into a portable, interoperable format", "why": "OKF 정의"}
{"id": "e100", "source": "w4", "locator": "§Three principles", "quote": "OKF requires exactly one thing of every concept: a type field.", "why": "최소 요구"}
{"id": "e101", "source": "w4", "locator": "§How OKF works", "quote": "Bundles can optionally include index.md files (for progressive disclosure as agents navigate the hierarchy) and log.md files (for chronological history of changes).", "why": "progressive disclosure 용 index.md"}
{"id": "e102", "source": "c1", "locator": "§Key terms", "quote": "Gate: the rule that decides whether a proposed skill edit should become the current skill.", "why": "gate 정의"}
{"id": "e103", "source": "c1", "locator": "§3.1", "quote": "In a paired study with gpt-5.4-nano on SearchQA, the ungated run adopted a plausible but wrong rule—answer with the document title string verbatim—and fell from 55.4% to 2.6%. The gated run rejected all proposals and remained flat at 57.0%.", "why": "무게이트 붕괴 사례"}
{"id": "e104", "source": "c1", "locator": "§3.1", "quote": "The two runs started from different measured baselines, so this is not evidence that they encountered identical candidate edits; it is an observed stress-case contrast.", "why": "저자 단서"}
{"id": "e105", "source": "c1", "locator": "§Part II", "quote": "that judgment can route a likely Skill Defect toward a targeted skill-body update and an Execution Lapse toward a protected appendix reminder", "why": "결함 귀속 두 갈래"}
{"id": "e106", "source": "c1", "locator": "§2.1", "quote": "gpt-5.4-mini | Spreadsheet | -13.8% | +4.7%", "why": "넓은 기억이 작은 모델을 망침"}
{"id": "e107", "source": "c1", "locator": "§2.2", "quote": "the absolute score changes are +9.65% on mini SearchQA, +15.00% on mini SpreadsheetBench, and +2.32% on nano SpreadsheetBench", "why": "consolidation 회복"}
{"id": "e108", "source": "c1", "locator": "§Part III", "quote": "Normal operation does not replace the deployed skill until the user explicitly runs adopt; auto_adopt is an opt-in mode.", "why": "staged adoption"}
{"id": "e109", "source": "c1", "locator": "§Evidence and reproducibility boundary", "quote": "Its raw per-run artifacts are not included in the public repository, so this post is not a reproduction package for those ablations.", "why": "재현 한계"}
{"id": "e110", "source": "c1", "locator": "§3.4", "quote": "The Sleep study is single-seed per cell; treat differences below 1.5 percentage points as noise", "why": "단일 seed"}
{"id": "e111", "source": "c2", "locator": "§intro", "quote": "Employees ask our internal knowledge base more than 15,000 questions every day.", "why": "Cerebras 규모"}
